{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented as Gerrit change 2256 —\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2256 (commit 259a645961fc, branch\n`e668-mutation-sandbox`). Not closing until Verified +1 AND merged.\n\n## What landed\n\n- **`scripts/mutation_sandbox.py`** (144 LOC) — mechanism probe, Seatbelt profile\n  generation, `bwrap` argv construction, fail-closed `wrap()`, and `sandbox_env()`.\n- **`scripts/mutation_gate.py`** — both shard-test-executing subprocesses in\n  `execute_shard` wrapped: the baseline `pytest` and the `mutmut run` mutant test-run.\n  778 LOC, under the 800 cap, which is why the logic lives in its own module.\n- **`tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py`** — 14 tests.\n- **`docs/local-dev-env.md`** — operator note on `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED`.\n\n## The mutation check found a real gap in my own tests\n\nAfter wiring, I seeded two defects to check the tests had teeth:\n\n1. Removing `--max-children 1` → the existing concurrency assertion went RED. Good.\n2. **Removing the sandbox wrap from the `mutmut run` call → all 42 tests stayed\n   GREEN.** The enforcement tests proved the *module* denies, but nothing bound it to\n   the call site, so deleting the control was invisible.\n\nThat is the AC this ticket wrote and my first cut did not satisfy. Closed it with\nthree call-site-binding tests (`test_the_mutmut_run_subprocess_is_sandbox_wrapped`\nand siblings). Re-seeding defect 2 now fails with a message naming the incident.\n\n## Enforcement is observed, not asserted\n\nThe live tests execute under the sandbox and check the filesystem afterward rather\nthan inspecting argv — argv assertions would pass against a sandbox that denies\nnothing. Measured on macOS 26.5.2: write outside the allow-list denied and file\nabsent; write inside succeeded; `rm -rf <protected>/*` denied with the target\nsurviving. They skip where no mechanism exists, so Linux `bwrap` enforcement remains\nunverified until the ubuntu CI leg is green — the asymmetry this ticket's ACs state.\n\n## Collateral fix\n\n`tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`'s `mutmut_run_concurrency` helper required\n`_run`'s first argument to be a literal `ast.Tuple`; the wrapper made it a `Call`, so\nits `--max-children` assertion silently matched nothing. Taught it to look through\nthe wrap — verified still RED when `--max-children` is removed, so the assertion kept\nits strength rather than being loosened.\n\n## Verification\n\n`make lint` 0, `make typecheck` 0, complexity ratchet 0, 56 tests pass across the\nsandbox and existing harness suites."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787801595629876001,"uuid":"eb77a8f2-f081-4bd1-9193-df0d2672e058"}